{"title":"2000 CEMC Gauss (Grade 8) Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_18\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 18</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/1/821091b44f7b71be1ed43de86eab3a0a94fc753f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{5} + 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a4352098b1382696f05ab2c98965328804895881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 20 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 37 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 11 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 13 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A number is placed in the box to make the following statement true: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/4/c24454ebba726cc793b902073ef11221d8f3083c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8+\\frac{7}{\\square}+\\frac{3}{1000} =8.073.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"184\" height=\"38\" /> What is this number?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/08196e4d2b41d7c0a2dcbcf6fbc2adea94582ba3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 1000 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 100 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 1 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 10 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 70$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"452\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/c/88c340879234ac4ae9de8955c2d65a33cee594d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5+4-3}{5+4+3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"78\" height=\"40\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/4/5b4d93a9ade8d46b99e047d6f08392ce649fe74b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ -1 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ \\frac{1}{3} \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ -\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"444\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Please add the next problems if anyone can\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Pat planned to place patio stones in a rectangular garden that has dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> m by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> m.  If each patio stone measures <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> m by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" /> m, how many stones are needed to cover the garden? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/b/6fbdb973cd4142db2d4c638f6944a5bcc335d9ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 240 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 180 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 120 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 60 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"461\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The prime numbers between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> are added together to form the number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" />.  What is the largest prime divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/5/5351d296b5674cb8207a306f4412527dab730631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/1/2c1845fb13d048f7c9eebbe5ba1b1816e663e258.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 2 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 3 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 5 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 7 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"397\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A set of five different positive integers has an average (arithmetic mean) of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/7/4e76ce9da0f428536412a4f539b127c608760686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"21\" height=\"12\" />  What is the largest possible number in this set?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/7/e7742cff1f848ad79f5109bdc3f0657731da528d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 45 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 35 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 44 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 46$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_18\">Problem 18</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2000_CEMC_Gauss_(Grade_8)_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 18\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Jim drives 60 km south, 40 km west, 20 km north, and 10 km east.  What is the distance from his starting point to his finishing point?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/f/baff12efaab47c025348972ba195f285874ac232.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 30 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 50 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 40 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 70 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 35$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"433\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017191347\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 116/10